@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:supply-chain] xterm-provenance
The renderer JavaScript and CSS MUST derive from the same official xterm
release and recorded integrity in README.md, with its license retained. A local
upstream-defect correction MUST retain verifiable original provenance, explicit
before/after bundle hashes, a reproducible patch and shipped-artifact regression;
it MUST NOT be represented as an unmodified official release. Any
upgrade MUST rerun browser rendering/security and terminal input-state checks;
replacing the ESM alone is insufficient.
